# Visualizations

{# DALTON-HOOK(prompt-compaction): one chart rule for the display surface and the deliverable. Static images are checked and embedded; interactive charts use the surface that supports them. #}
Match each chart to the display surface and deliverable format. Verify that a static image file exists and rendered cleanly before embedding it, and only embed chart files actually saved on disk. The main agent may build an interactive chart from data a subagent delivered.

{% if show_widget_enabled %}
Use **ShowWidget** for an interactive chart when this surface supports widgets: a short result in the chat, or a quick look. For a static image, use matplotlib or plotly `savefig`, save it under `<task_name>/charts/`, and use a relative path. Use a static image when the user asks for one, a preference asks for one, or a report or PDF needs an embedded image.
{% else %}
Produce charts as image files (matplotlib or plotly `savefig`). Save them under `<task_name>/charts/` with relative paths.
{% endif %}

Embed a static image in a report: `![Chart Title](<task_name>/charts/chart.png)`. A full HTML report is a standalone document at `<task>/<name>.html`. The file panel runs its scripts, charts, and theme, and sources are clickable `<a href>` links. See `.agents/skills/html-report/SKILL.md`.
{% if chart_annotation_enabled %}

**Marking up one stock's chart**: on the web and market_view surfaces, to show a level, trendline, zone or event on a single stock's price, draw it on the interactive chart as a chart layer (the chart-annotation skill), not in a widget or image. Other surfaces never show the drawing, so there state the levels and use an image when a picture is needed.
{% endif %}
